","isError":false,"requestId":""}}},"draftExchange":{"request_message":"Implement a segment-based territorial control system for bot navigation with the following requirements:

1. **Segment Occupation Broadcasting System**:
 - Each bot should continuously broadcast which NavSegment (from PathBerserker2d) they currently occupy
 - Create a centralized segment occupation manager that tracks which bot occupies which segment
 - Update occupation data in real-time as bots move between segments

2. **Territory Control Rules**:
 - **Enemy bots**: Completely prohibited from entering segments occupied by opposing team members (hard restriction)
 - **Allied bots**: Discouraged from entering segments occupied by teammates (soft restriction with increased pathfinding cost)

3. **PathBerserker2d Integration**:
 - Modify the pathfinding system to respect segment occupation rules
 - Use NavAgent's segment detection capabilities to determine current bot positions
 - Integrate with PathBerserker2d's cost system to make occupied segments expensive/forbidden

4. **Implementation Requirements**:
 - Extend BotManager to handle segment occupation tracking
 - Modify CustomFollower to report current segment and respect occupation rules
 - Implement efficient segment lookup and occupation checking
 - Add visualization for occupied segments (different colors for ally/enemy occupied)

5. **Performance Considerations**:
 - Minimize Update loop overhead for segment tracking
 - Use events or callbacks for segment changes rather than continuous polling
 - Cache segment occupation data to avoid repeated lookups

6. **Fallback Behavior**:
 - Define what happens when no valid path exists due to segment occupation
 - Implement waiting/queuing system for contested segments
 - Add timeout mechanisms to prevent permanent blocking

Restructure the CustomFollower script and related components to implement this segment-based territorial navigation system while maintaining clean code architecture and optimal performance.","rich_text_json_repr":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Implement a segment-based territorial control system for bot navigation with the following requirements:"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"1. **Segment Occupation Broadcasting System**:"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Each bot should continuously broadcast which NavSegment (from PathBerserker2d) they currently occupy"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Create a centralized segment occupation manager that tracks which bot occupies which segment"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Update occupation data in real-time as bots move between segments"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"2. **Territory Control Rules**:"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - **Enemy bots**: Completely prohibited from entering segments occupied by opposing team members (hard restriction)"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - **Allied bots**: Discouraged from entering segments occupied by teammates (soft restriction with increased pathfinding cost)"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"3. **PathBerserker2d Integration**:"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Modify the pathfinding system to respect segment occupation rules"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Use NavAgent's segment detection capabilities to determine current bot positions"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Integrate with PathBerserker2d's cost system to make occupied segments expensive/forbidden"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"4. **Implementation Requirements**:"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Extend BotManager to handle segment occupation tracking"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Modify CustomFollower to report current segment and respect occupation rules"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Implement efficient segment lookup and occupation checking"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Add visualization for occupied segments (different colors for ally/enemy occupied)"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"5. **Performance Considerations**:"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Minimize Update loop overhead for segment tracking"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Use events or callbacks for segment changes rather than continuous polling"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Cache segment occupation data to avoid repeated lookups"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"6. **Fallback Behavior**:"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Define what happens when no valid path exists due to segment occupation"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Implement waiting/queuing system for contested segments"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":" - Add timeout mechanisms to prevent permanent blocking"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Restructure the CustomFollower script and related components to implement this segment-based territorial navigation system while maintaining clean code architecture and optimal performance."}]}]},"mentioned_items":[],"status":"draft"},"requestIds":[],"isPinned":false,"isShareable":true,"extraData":{"isAgentConversation":true,"hasDirtyEdits":true},"personaType":0,"rootTaskUuid":"1a93a23a-2191-4884-9f0b-33b2a2a097bf"}},"agentExecutionMode":"manual","isPanelCollapsed":true,"displayedAnnouncements":[]}
